The change simplifies the conditional logic by combining the null check and validity check into a single short-circuit expression, avoiding an explicit branch and reducing instruction count. This improves performance by enabling better branch prediction and reducing code size.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsHrCalcTypeValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(5);
        return (field != FIT_NULL) && field->IsValueValid();
    }
```